.TH BIALET 1 "2026-11-09" "bialet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bialet \- full-stack web framework with embedded Wren and SQLite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bialet
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIAPPDIR\fR]
.br
.B bialet dev
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bialet
serves the application directory as a web site. Each
.I .wren
file in the directory is a route handler that returns a response body. The
server, the Wren interpreter, and an SQLite database live in one binary, with
no configuration files and no separate runtime.
.PP
With no arguments it serves the current directory on 127.0.0.1:7001. The
argument after the options, if given, selects a different application
directory.
.PP
The subcommand
.B dev
enables live reload and the in-browser error display, and opens the server URL
in a browser. Both are on for that run only: nothing is written to the
database, so a later plain \fBbialet\fR start, or a copy of
\fI_db.sqlite3\fR, has neither unless \fIBIALET_LIVE_RELOAD\fR or
\fIBIALET_SHOW_ERRORS\fR is set with \fBConfig.enable\fR.
.PP
While either is on, any client that can reach the port gets the error type,
module path, line and message of a failing handler, and \fI/_livereload\fR is
public. Use \fBbialet dev\fR on a development machine only, never in
production.
.PP
Bialet speaks HTTP/1.1, one request per connection (\fIConnection: close\fR),
and does not terminate TLS. Put nginx, Apache, or Caddy in front for HTTPS,
HTTP/2, and rate limiting.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option has a short and a long form; values may be passed as
\fB\-\-option value\fR or \fB\-\-option=value\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIPORT\fR"
Port to listen on. Default: 7001.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-host " \fIHOST\fR"
Host name or address to bind. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run " \fICODE\fR"
Run the Wren code passed as the argument, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-validate " \fIFILE\fR"
Validate the syntax of a Wren file, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tests
Run the tests in the \fI_tests/\fR folder.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-log " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the log to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-db " \fIFILE\fR"
SQLite database file. Default: \fI_db.sqlite3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wal
Enable SQLite write-ahead logging.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore " \fIGLOBS\fR"
Comma-separated list of glob patterns of files to ignore.
Default: \fIREADME*,AGENTS*,LICENSE*,*.json,*.yml,*.yaml,*.exe\fR.
The list replaces the default one; repeat the defaults to keep them.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mem\-soft " \fIMB\fR"
Soft memory limit in MB (Linux only; see \fIdocs/security.md\fR). Default: 128.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-mem\-hard " \fIMB\fR"
Hard memory limit in MB. Default: 256.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cpu\-soft " \fISECONDS\fR"
CPU time soft limit of the HTTP process, in seconds (not a percentage).
Reaching it sends SIGXCPU and the supervisor starts a fresh process.
0 means no limit. Default: 3600.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cpu\-hard " \fISECONDS\fR"
CPU time hard limit, in seconds; reaching it sends SIGKILL. Default: 7200.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-max\-post " \fIKB\fR"
Maximum request body size in KB. Default: 128.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-max\-upload\-size " \fISIZE\fR"
Maximum size per uploaded file in bytes; a
.B K
,
.B M
, or
.B G
suffix scales it. Default: 4M.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreign\-keys " \fION|OFF\fR"
SQLite foreign key enforcement. Default: on.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-synchronous " \fILEVEL\fR"
SQLite synchronous mode: off, normal, full, or extra. Default: normal.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-secret\-key\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Deployment key for \fBConfig.encrypt\fR and \fBConfig.decrypt\fR: 64 hex
characters (an AES-256 key) or a passphrase. The file must be a regular file
outside the app root; keep it readable only by the server's user.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the browser auto-open and colored output.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-cache
Cache compiled user .wren files in memory (served files and local imports).
The framework module is always cached.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the application in the current directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bialet
.RE
.fi
.PP
Serve another directory on all interfaces, port 8080:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bialet \-h 0.0.0.0 \-p 8080 /path/to/app
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start in development mode:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bialet dev
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I _db.sqlite3
Default SQLite database, created next to the application files.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation at https://bialet.dev.
